# Keep local secrets out of the image. The Dockerfile's `COPY . .` would
# otherwise bake developer credentials into every layer.
#
# Nothing at runtime needs these: apps/api and apps/worker resolve /app/.env at
# startup, and dotenv treats a missing file as a no-op, so Fly's injected
# secrets are used instead.
.env
.env.*

# Version control and CI definitions.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Dependencies are installed inside the image by `pnpm install`, and copying the
# host's tree would clobber that (and drag in platform-specific binaries).
**/node_modules

# Build outputs and caches, all regenerated by `pnpm turbo build`.
# .turbo must be excluded together with dist: a stale local cache could convince
# turbo the build is already satisfied and skip emitting dist into the image.
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/coverage

# Local-only tooling configs, docs, and deploy manifests. These are read from
# the developer's machine or by the Fly/Netlify CLIs, never from inside the image.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
fly.api.toml
fly.worker.toml
netlify.toml
docs
plans
README.md

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.log
.vscode
.idea
